{"name":"Pencil Sketch","hex":"#999d9e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pencil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A writing utensil with a graphite (commonly referred to as lead) shaft, usually blended with clay, clad in wood, and sharpened to a taper. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An aggregate or collection of rays of light, especially when diverging from, or converging to, a point."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To write (something) using a pencil.","To mark with, or as if with, a pencil."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pencil"},{"term":"sketch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a brief, basic drawing.","To describe briefly and with very few details."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rapidly executed freehand drawing that is not intended as a finished work, often consisting of a multitude of overlapping lines.","A rough design, plan, or draft, as a rough draft of a book."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sketch (drawing)","blocks":[{"text":"A sketch is a rapidly executed freehand drawing that is not usually intended as a finished work. A sketch may serve a number of purposes: it might record something that the artist sees, it might record or develop an idea for later use or it might be used as a quick way of graphically demonstrating an image, idea or principle. Sketching is the most inexpensive art medium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Jesus_und_Ehebrecherin.jpg/330px-Jesus_und_Ehebrecherin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sketch_(drawing)","wikidata":"Q5078274"},{"title":"Pencil","blocks":[{"text":"A pencil is a writing or drawing implement with a solid pigment core in a protective casing that reduces the risk of core breakage and keeps it from marking the user's hand."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Pencils_hb.jpg/330px-Pencils_hb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pencil","wikidata":"Q14674"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Study_of_willows_by_Thomas_Gainsborough.jpg/500px-Study_of_willows_by_Thomas_Gainsborough.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Study_of_willows_by_Thomas_Gainsborough.jpg/500px-Study_of_willows_by_Thomas_Gainsborough.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charcoal sketch of willows by Thomas Gainsborough","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStudy_of_willows_by_Thomas_Gainsborough.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Artist%27s_Gridded_Sketch_of_Senenmut_MET_36.3.252_EGDP013666.jpg/250px-Artist%27s_Gridded_Sketch_of_Senenmut_MET_36.3.252_EGDP013666.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Artist%27s_Gridded_Sketch_of_Senenmut_MET_36.3.252_EGDP013666.jpg/330px-Artist%27s_Gridded_Sketch_of_Senenmut_MET_36.3.252_EGDP013666.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Artist%27s_Gridded_Sketch_of_Senenmut_MET_36.3.252_EGDP013666.jpg/250px-Artist%27s_Gridded_Sketch_of_Senenmut_MET_36.3.252_EGDP013666.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArtist's_Gridded_Sketch_of_Senenmut_MET_36.3.252_EGDP013666.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Leonardo_da_vinci%2C_Study_for_the_trivulzio_monument_02.jpg/120px-Leonardo_da_vinci%2C_Study_for_the_trivulzio_monument_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_